            "CLASS I": {
                "__levelup": {
                    "Mechanism of action": [
                        "They primarily limit the conductance of Na<sup>+</sup> (and K<sup>+</sup>) across cell membrane i.e, exerts local anaesthetic action.",
                        "They also reduce rate of phase 0 - depolarization in automatic cells.",
                        "They exert <b>'Use dependent' blockade</b> action i.e., acts more on rapidly firing fibres.",
                        [
                            {
                                "__type": "bullet"
                            },
                            "Thus, they block more on partially depolarized fibres."
                        ]
